  "body": "﻿#3999 has merged; this branch refreshes against `main` and is retargeted. The editor work for the multiaxis page rides the stacked PR for #2827.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **The parity proof.** `rotary_field_parity.rs` proves `Stock::simulate_rotary` against the independently written swept-ball/flute law for `OpParams::RotaryFlow`, at the verdict class, beside the Parallel/Contour/Offset lanes. A `Kind::Flow` fixture joins `common/rotary_bar.rs`: the laid bar, 72 facets (the density the band suite proves on - a 16-gon ring's 22.5 deg knots swing the pose past the kernel guard's drift margin), the band picked between the neck ring at x 2 and the top cap rim at x 16 - the pair whose feature chains advance about the axis in the same sense.\r\n- **The lift.** `stock_sim_rotary::rotary_kind_lift` answers `Ok(())` for `RotaryFlow` on the measured parity. The eye (`stock_view`, `stock_play`) cuts the kind; the column verdict still refuses it by name, as it refuses every rotary kind. `ROTARY_KIND_UNMEASURED` stays for the next kind; no kind carries it today.\r\n- **The radial C unwind.** `stamp_spindle_c`'s boolean became the enum `Unwind { NoProof, Axial, Radial }`: Rotary Contour unwinds over the axial plane, Rotary Flow on the retract cylinder, Parallel and Offset are refused where they would rewind - by name, the words now naming both proven kinds. `cl::unwind_c`'s cut-reach reading gained the mirror of its own plunge-start rule: a feed a rapid follows ENDED at rest, not in a cut, so the flow kernel's cut-feed exit off a pass no longer poisons the rest cylinder. Every inserted orbit chord is still judged by the verifier, the solid bar and the post gate.\r\n\r\n## The parity readings (release, the laid bar's neck band)\r\n\r\n- `Stock::simulate_rotary`: 2,063 moves, 1,559 turning -> 35,491 sub-chords, half-angle 1.990e-3, centre sag 5.940e-6 (within the 1e-4 pose law), wall 46.6 s, 1.312 ms per sub-chord.\r\n- Height parity: 168 sphere-cut tops within **1.269e-5** of the law, bound **2.011e-5** (centre sag 5.94e-6 + `FIELD_VERDICT_EPS` 1e-5 + the law's sampling sag 4.2e-6); 1,015 standing tops exact; 0 flute-cut, 0 grazing, 0 sliver columns.\r\n- Sign parity: 7,053 probed cell centres, **0 misses**, worst 0.000e0, band 1.832e-2.\r\n- The eye's own class: 2,131 sub-chords in 3.0 s (1.414 ms each).\r\n\r\nNo epsilon was widened; `FIELD_VERDICT_EPS` and the sag bounds stand as the other kinds left them. The readings and the fixture's band choice are recorded in `docs/decisions/2828-rotaryflow-parity.md`.\r\n\r\n## The pins\r\n\r\n- `cl::rotary_unwind`: a feed-retract link shape (the flow kernel's own) unwinds at its cylinder with `radial = true`, is refused by name without it; the at-or-inside-the-cut-radius refusals still refuse.\r\n- `rotary_gate` unit pins: the gate unwinds the radial path for Rotary Flow (a stated C rate given, #906), refuses it for Rotary Contour, refuses Parallel/Offset by name.\r\n- `rotary_flow_band`: the full-ring band on the shipped millturn (C -360..360, stated rates) generates, unwinds at its radial retract links, every C inside the travel, the chain held, C continuous, a rewind orbit spanning a whole turn on the retract cylinder; a stated travel with no C rate refuses the rewind by name (#906); a pass wider than a narrow travel refuses with no clear link inside it.\r\n- `rotary_field_parity` quick tests: the column verdict refuses Flow by name; the eye draws the lifted kind.\r\n\r\n## What was not exercised\r\n\r\n- The two new heavy lanes (`the_flow_kind_reads_the_radial_law`, `the_flow_kinds_eye_cost_is_measured`) are `#[ignore]`d and run at the cut; both were run locally in release to take the readings above.\r\n- Posting the unwound flow band through the lathe post is held out: the radial field law reads the ball on the band's convex crease ring as a gouge past its allowance - the finding #2826 already reports, and that warning blocks the post of a clean unwind.\r\n- The flow unwind tests joined `rotary_flow_band.rs`, not `c_axis_unwind.rs`: `c_axis_unwind.rs` sits at 356 lines and the flow fixtures (band picks, bench C) already live in the flow suite. Both gate modules' unit tests moved to sibling files (`rotary_gate_tests.rs`, `rotary_unwind_tests.rs`) to hold the 400-line law. A top-level test binary was added: `rotary_flow_band.rs`. Reason: the band fixtures and grammar pins span the motion kernel, the app project grammar and posting; their natural siblings in the flow suite are already top-level.\r\n- The editor findings (items 1-4 of the review: screenshots, the stated-axis arm, the retract-radius control, the tilt wording) land via the stacked PR for #2827, whose branch owns `crates/ui/src/egui_app/multiaxis_page.rs`; its screenshots cover the before/after views. This PR's breaking-change commit is `0085ba36e` (`BREAKING CHANGE:` footer: the project file moves from v81 to v82; a v81 reader refuses the new files).\r\n- The `graphify update` step did not run: the graphify binary is not installed in this environment; `graphify-out/` is generated output and nothing committed reads it.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Rotary Flow: the field eye now cuts the kind (parity proved against the radial law), and on a spindle C with stated travel the band unwinds by whole turns at its radial retract links instead of refusing.\r\n\r\nFixes #2828\r\n\r\n",
